https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260322075917.254874-1-alex.popov@linux.com/T/#u"|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31695|0.00000|0.00000|0.0000
  CVE-2026-31694|2026-05-01T14:16:19.133|2026-05-01T15:24:14.893|0.0|NONE|N/A|N/A|false|"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:

fuse: reject oversized dirents in page cache

fuse_add_dirent_to_cache() computes a serialized dirent size from the
server-controlled namelen field and copies the dirent into a single
page-cache page. The existing logic only checks whether the dirent fits
in the remaining space of the current page and advances to a fresh page
if not. It never checks whether the dirent itself exceeds PAGE_SIZE.

As a result, a malicious FUSE server can return a dirent with
namelen=4095, producing a serialized record size of 4120 bytes. On 4 KiB
page systems this causes memcpy() to overflow the cache page by 24 bytes
into the following kernel page.

Reject dirents that cannot fit in a single page before copying them into
the readdir cache."|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31694|0.00000|0.00000|0.0000
  CVE-2026-7581|2026-05-01T13:15:59.477|2026-05-01T15:26:24.553|2.1|LOW|CWE-346|N/A|false|A security vulnerability has been detected in alexta69 MeTube up to 2026.04.09. This affects the function on_prepare of the file app/main.py of the component CORS Policy. The manipulation leads to permissive cross-domain policy with untrusted domains. The attack is possible to be carried out remotely. The exploit has been disclosed publicly and may be used. Upgrading to version 2026.04.10 is able to mitigate this issue. The identifier of the patch is 0072d3488ae5b8d922d3ee87458d829993742a32. It is recommended to upgrade the affected component.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-7581|0.00000|0.00000|1.4700
